plugin-hostd-protocol (0.8.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Revert the chain-2 fold (V16, #137) and its catalog fix: it waits for
    chain 3
  * check-catalogs: translate names the domain plugin-hostd, whose words the
    catalogs hold
  * scenarios: curve_bind terms spell the standard unit ids dB and Hz, and
    the seed corpus and the golden transcript are written again by their
    generators
  * codec: a reply code's sentence is also read from the domain that keeps it
  * test: the no-domain arm of grouping_reasons_test hides the installed
    contract directory too
  * the old-home grep: plugin-db's pin and db files are named by their domain
  * packaging: the plugin-db-contract floor stays at the released 0.4.4
  * tests: the empty-directory arm of param-scales holds the installed
    contract out
  * packaging: every floor on a package this delivery releases is its
    delivered version
  * V16: the word tests render this tree's domains as check-domain-renders
    does, contract.d and then the installed contract directory
  * fuzz: GRAMMAR.sha256 is the merged grammar's
  * V16: the renders of this tree's domains read the installed contract
    directory beside contract.d, omx-clap-contract >= 0.35.0 their floor
  * V16: the renders of this tree's domains resolve a reference to an
    installed owner's domain, a test that fails while they read contract.d
    alone (red)
  * check-rendered: plugin-db's vocabulary is the render of its domain
    plugin-db, and the two omx-clap headers and it are rendered again from
    the chain-1 producers
  * grammar: curve-unit takes either case, the standard unit ids curve_bind
    takes since 116e042
  * grammar: every standard unit id of omx-dsp's OMX_CURVE_UNITS_STANDARD is
    a curve-unit, a test that fails while the rule takes lower case only (red)
  * estimate_words_test reads PARAM_UNITS from omx-contract's domain param,
    not from a primitives.json omx-contract no longer installs
  * V29: the rendered omx-clap vocabulary header holds HOSTING_VERB_HOSTS,
    omx-clap's
  * V29: the two rendered host verb headers name their hosts' item
    HOSTING_VERB_HOSTS, omx-clap's
  * V16: the codecs read the protocol's sentences from the domains alone,
    never from a 3/<package>/verbs.json
  * V16: a stale 3/plugin-hostd-protocol/verbs.json beside the domain is
    never read by the codecs, a test that fails while they read it first (red)
  * V16: the words of the protocol are the domain plugin-hostd, and
    data/verbs.json is gone
  * V16: the words of the protocol are read from the domain plugin-hostd, a
    test that fails while they are in data/verbs.json (red)
  * codec fixtures: the estimate reply with its verdict and reason is read,
    with a code that has no name and an unknown plugin
  * the generated pin and estimate lists carry a doc comment, so the doxygen
    gate holds
  * the seed corpus of the grammar is written again after the estimate words
    join the tree
  * estimate: the CPU ceiling is the domain's scalar ESTIMATE_CPU_CEILING,
    rendered into protocol.h
  * tests: the CPU ceiling of the insert verdict is the domain's scalar,
    rendered by the generator (red)
  * codec: the TypeScript codec's estimate test reads the verdict and its
    reason
  * estimate: the host's insert verdict is a word of the domain estimate, and
    the reply ends with it
  * tests: the insert verdict of estimate is the host's, its words generated
    from the domain estimate (red)
  * curve_bind: a term's unit is a standard id, read from omx-dsp's
    CURVE_UNITS standard names
  * plugin-hostd-protocol 0.8.0: VERSION, the spec, debian/changelog and
    package.json
  * history_get: its words are the domain plugin-hostd/history, not
    data/history.json
  * omx-clap domains: the shared verbs are read from contract.d/omx-clap and
    contract.d/host
  * omx-clap rename: the origin word and the prose name omx-clap
  * omx-clap rename: read the new names
  * ci: every pull request body closes an issue
  * V12: the vendored plugin_db_vocabulary.h is re-rendered without the pin
    verdict and pool items
  * V17: GroupingReason and RETRY_REASONS of both clients are written from
    plugin-hostd's domain plugin-hostd/grouping
  * V21: PHD_PARAM_SCALES is written from omx-contract's domain param,
    protocol.h spells no scale word
  * V12: the pin verdict and pool words are this package's domain,
    protocol.h's pin words are generated from it
  * V8: the probe words are this package's domain, protocol.h's lists are
    generated from it
  * Python client: command() and reply() speak through plugin_hostd_protocol
    (#34)
  * tests: the Python client's command() and reply() go through the codec
    (#34, red)
  * Python codec: the NUL helper's docstring passes the ruff documentation
    gate
  * Python client and codec refuse a NUL: it is the protocol's line end

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Mon, 23 Nov 2026 20:54:19 +0000
